name\": name, \"email\": email})\n}\n\nNeed refactor. External behavior identical: status codes, response bodies. Note original success response: Content-Type application/json, body JSON object with name/email plus trailing newline from Encoder. Error responses: no Content-Type set, body exact bytes. Need preserve. If we use helper writeJSON? For errors, must not set Content-Type? Original doesn't set Content-Type for errors. If helper sets Content-Type for all, external behavior changes (headers). User says same status codes, same response bodies, not necessarily headers? But likely keep identical external behavior including headers? They specifically status codes and response bodies. But safer preserve headers too: errors no Content-Type, success Content-Type. Could have writeError(w, status, message) writes status and exact body no content type. writeUserJSON sets content type and encodes. But JSON encoding separated into testable function? Could have encodeUser(w, user) or userJSON(user) ([]byte, error). But to keep exact body, use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(user) which adds newline. If we use json.Marshal, body lacks newline. Need preserve.", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0008756775059737265], [22916, -7.86430549621582]], [[1144, -1.4662849935120903e-05], [513, -12.068293571472168]], [[4087, -0.010461261495947838], [310, -5.000152111053467]], [[1156, -0.02704750746488571], [303, -3.9276211261749268]], [[579, -0.27390316128730774], [25, -2.2489359378814697]], [[1622, -0.003313302295282483], [3296, -6.571932315826416]], [[13, -0.37708526849746704], [25, -1.5233443975448608]], [[14235, -0.03014848381280899], [1165, -4.172055244445801]], [[89109, -0.29549890756607056], [7936, -1.8288451433181763]], [[5805, -0.000244468537857756], [2400, -8.746906280517578]], [[9830, -0.02760726399719715], [6795, -3.6704599857330322]], [[6795, -3.171017306158319e-05], [17369, -11.887532234191895]], [[47781, -1.416580080986023], [1083, -1.6446207761764526]], [[4475, -0.999129056930542], [2833, 